                    <p class="">Qur'an | 96:1</p>
                </div>

            </div>
            <p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
            @* End Qoute Section 1 *@

          
            <p>These verses illustrate that education and seeking knowledge are not only commendable but also a means of raising one’s status. </p>
            <p>Many scholars allude to the concept  that education is the essence of knowledge. Seeking knowledge and gaining a good Islamic education is a means of strengthening our Iman, understanding and relationship with Allah. </p>
            <p>Seeking knowledge is a means of having our sins forgiven and attaining huge reward: </p>
            @* Start Qoute Section*@
            <div class="" style="padding-bottom:50px;margin-top:30px;">

                <div class="quote-container col-md-12">
                    <span class="" style="font-size:4em;font-weight:bold">&lsquo;&lsquo;</span>
                    <p class="quote">
                        Whoever treads on a path in search of Islamic knowledge, Allah will ease the way to Paradise for him. The angels will lower their wings, pleased with this seeker of knowledge, and everyone in the heavens and on earth will ask forgiveness for the knowledgeable person, even the fish in the deepest of waters will ask for his forgiveness.
                    </p>
                    <p class="">Hadith | Abu Dawud</p>
                </div>

            </div>
            @* End Qoute Section*@
            <p>&nbsp;</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-3"></div>
    </div>
